1
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:11,640
Daddy, please don't shoot Mommy.

2
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:12,880
‎PREVIOUSLY

3
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:16,400
Please ask me to do something else.
I can't kill someone.

4
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:17,440
If you don't help me,

5
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:18,520
I'll expose you.

6
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:21,400
If I don't kill him, he'll drag me
straight to prison.

7
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:24,600
Grandpa left everything to Hathaya.

8
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,960
Dead people can't talk.

9
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:13,280
Grandpa.

10
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:26,520
Aren't you happy

11
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:29,160
to see your favorite granddaughter?

12
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:36,120
Of course.

13
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:40,920
Ever since Hathaya moved into this house,

14
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:44,160
I've been pushed aside.

15
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:08,240
Grandpa.

16
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:13,480
I'm sorry

17
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:16,240
I disappointed you.

18
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:19,800
I tried to fix everything.

19
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:21,440
I wanted to make you proud.

20
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:24,160
But Raiwin is useless.

21
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:26,360
He ruined everything.

22
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,720
I'm sorry

23
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:36,480
I caused you to end up
bedridden like this.

24
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:41,080
I feel terrible.

25
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:44,480
I don't want you to suffer anymore.

26
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:54,960
Grandpa never threw anything away.

27
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,240
He kept everything exactly the same.

28
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:03,120
Grandpa still loves me.

29
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:10,560
Lying here sick like this

30
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:13,360
must be so uncomfortable.

31
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:28,240
Chayanee.

32
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:30,720
Help. Help me.

33
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:33,400
Chayanee.

34
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:36,480
Help me…

35
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:39,320
Grandpa, you can talk.

36
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:42,280
Help.

37
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:56,800
AESOP'S FABLES

38
00:06:56,880 --> 00:07:00,160
Chayanee, Grandpa can talk now.
Let's get out of here.

39
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:01,400
-Quickly.
-Mom, help me.

40
00:07:04,080 --> 00:07:05,720
Let's go, sweetheart.

41
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:07,720
Help me.

42
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:13,120
When I was little,

43
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:18,280
Grandpa used to read me stories
that taught me to be strong.

44
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:23,640
Now I'll read them to him.

45
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:25,600
Help me.

46
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:28,120
Someone's coming.

47
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:34,120
Miss Chayanee. Madam. Don't do this!

48
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:36,520
Shut up. I'll give you a million.

49
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:38,680
Go stand outside.
Don't let anyone come in.

50
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:41,720
Do you want to die?

51
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,960
-Go.
-Yes.

52
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:47,720
Mom, help me.

53
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:57,120
What are you doing here?

54
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,040
Well…

55
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:02,480
I was just going to clean the prayer room.

56
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:05,800
Then go ahead.

57
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:12,080
What is it? Why are you stopping me?

58
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:19,000
Miss Hathaya, please save Mr. Pichai.

59
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:22,160
Please…

60
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,600
Please help him.

61
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:25,280
He is going to die.

62
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:30,360
Quickly.

63
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:33,919
Chayanee! What are you doing?

64
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:38,039
Let go of him.

65
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:40,240
Chamoi, drag her out.

66
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,200
Let go.

67
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:43,240
Yes. I'll drag her out
just like you ordered.

68
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:45,240
What are you doing?

69
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:46,320
Grandpa.

70
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:48,240
Grandpa!

71
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:49,640
Just like you ordered.

72
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:51,680
Chamoi!

73
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:54,960
-Chayanee!
-Let go!

74
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:55,880
Let go of her.

75
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:58,200
Chayanee, did you try to kill Grandpa?

76
00:08:58,280 --> 00:08:59,840
If Grandpa dies,

77
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:01,640
everything he owns will become mine.

78
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:04,000
You're so meddlesome.

79
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:05,280
You can die too.

80
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:08,680
No. Don't!

81
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:10,440
-Chamoi!
-No!

82
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:12,680
You can't!

83
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:14,960
-What are you doing?
-Let go.

84
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,880
What is going on?!

85
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:20,720
Aunt Ann! Chayanee and
Aunt Liu are trying to kill Grandpa.

86
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:23,080
Call the police!

87
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:24,760
Okay.

88
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:28,160
Give me that.

89
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:31,800
Ann!

90
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:32,880
Here.

91
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:35,400
Call them.

92
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:40,880
It's hot!

93
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:43,520
Chayanee, run!

94
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:46,400
Hurry. Run!

95
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:49,960
I can't take this anymore.

96
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:52,040
Grandpa.

97
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:56,800
Grandpa. Grandpa!

98
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:59,480
Chayanee, what are we going to do?

99
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:01,560
The police are going to arrest us.

100
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:03,640
-I'm scared.
-Mom, stop panicking.

101
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:05,480
We need to get out before the police come.

102
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:09,360
Chayanee.

103
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:18,000
My dear.

104
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:20,680
Sweetheart.

105
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:24,720
Blood…

106
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:27,840
Mom, help me.

107
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:31,120
Sweetheart, hold on. We have to go.

108
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:35,920
Get up.

109
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:40,040
Chayanee.

110
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,320
Come on.

111
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:49,720
Grandpa, wake up.

112
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,320
Grandpa, wake up.

113
00:10:58,440 --> 00:11:01,480
Grandpa. I'm here.

114
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:04,680
I'm here now.

115
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,720
Grandpa.

116
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:12,400
Grandpa, you always taught me to fight.

117
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:14,920
So you have to fight too.

118
00:11:16,640 --> 00:11:18,480
Please, Grandpa.

119
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:22,640
I have no one left.

120
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:27,720
I don't have anyone else.

121
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:32,800
Please don't leave me.

122
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:35,200
Grandpa.

123
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:39,920
Grandpa.

124
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,920
Grandpa, wake up.

125
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:52,160
Grandpa. You're awake.

126
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,720
You're awake.

127
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:03,040
You don't have to be afraid anymore.

128
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:05,880
From now on, I'll protect you.

129
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:08,880
You don't have to be afraid anymore.

130
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:17,120
Grandpa.

131
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:24,960
My granddaughter.

132
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:27,640
Thank you.

133
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:32,000
My granddaughter.

134
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:37,160
Grandpa, you can talk.

135
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:46,400
Hathaya.

136
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:55,600
Grandpa, you can move your hand too.

137
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,280
Grandpa…

138
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:03,040
Stay with me, Grandpa.
Please stay with me.

139
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,520
I already filed a police report.

140
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:15,560
They're sending officers
to find Chayanee and Liu.

141
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:19,960
I never imagined

142
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:23,000
they would actually try to kill Grandpa.

143
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:25,320
Greed can blind people so badly

144
00:13:25,880 --> 00:13:27,040
that they're willing

145
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:29,440
to kill their own family.

146
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:37,320
Mr. Ramil.

147
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:42,360
Miss Hathaya.
Please don't send me to prison.

148
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:44,760
I'm not pressing charges against you.

149
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:48,080
If anything, I should thank you.
You changed your mind

150
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:50,320
and warned me in time to save Grandpa.

151
00:13:52,680 --> 00:13:53,920
I know

152
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,960
I'm not a good person.

153
00:13:57,040 --> 00:14:00,160
But I'm not so evil that I could stand by

154
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:02,560
while someone murders
a person I owe so much to.

155
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:05,960
Madam and Miss Chayanee

156
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,200
have done terrible things.

157
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:11,480
I wanted to speak up, but I couldn't.

158
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:13,640
I owed them too much.

159
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:15,760
But this was more than I could bear.

160
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:19,720
They're heartless beyond belief.

161
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:22,200
If you tell the police
everything you know,

162
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:27,160
I'll consider you a witness
helping the investigation.

163
00:14:30,560 --> 00:14:31,440
Well…

164
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:35,080
Madam and Miss Chayanee

165
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:37,560
were the ones

166
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:42,040
who arranged for Pong

167
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:44,560
to sexually assault
Miss Hathaya at the house

168
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:46,840
and at the construction site.

169
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:56,280
My mom

170
00:14:57,440 --> 00:14:59,320
was framed, wasn't she?

171
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:00,960
Yes.

172
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:04,480
Ms. Liu…

173
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:08,080
was the one behind it.

174
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:09,560
She had Pong

175
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:13,120
take your mother to the gambling den
and get her trapped in debt.

176
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:16,560
Then she arranged for your mother

177
00:15:17,160 --> 00:15:19,360
to steal the money from the office.

178
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:21,360
But…

179
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:24,720
karma is real.

180
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:26,520
What do you mean?

181
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:28,720
Pong threatened

182
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:31,120
to expose Madam's crimes.

183
00:15:31,880 --> 00:15:34,840
So Madam

184
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:37,760
planned to kill him.

185
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:44,400
We need to tell the police immediately.
If we find Pong,

186
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:46,840
it'll be easier to close the case.

187
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:49,040
Uh…

188
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:52,440
But Madam already killed him.

189
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:54,040
Pong is dead.

190
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,280
No.

191
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:58,200
Hathaya and I saved him.

192
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,480
But he escaped again.

193
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,640
What is it, Aunt Chamoi?

194
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:11,080
I hate to even think about it.

195
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:12,840
Pong…

196
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:16,960
is going to come after Madam for revenge.

197
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:23,080
Karma is real. Like they say,

198
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:26,280
whatever you do to others

199
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:28,240
eventually comes back to you.

200
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:38,560
-I'll be leaving.
-Yes.

201
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:40,240
Please excuse me.

202
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:54,720
The doctor said…

203
00:16:57,880 --> 00:16:59,040
you lost the baby.

204
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:07,560
I wanted to have a family.

205
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:13,000
I thought if I had a baby,

206
00:17:15,319 --> 00:17:16,480
Grandpa would love my child

207
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:19,079
the way he used to love me.

208
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:23,200
Now there's nothing left.

209
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:26,960
Everything is ruined.
My whole life is ruined.

210
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:31,640
Everything is gone, Mom.

211
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:38,840
Forget it, sweetheart.
Maybe it's for the best.

212
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:41,120
At least we won't have to raise a child

213
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,960
with their rotten blood.

214
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:48,160
Chayanee.

215
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:51,720
Don't think about anything right now.

216
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:54,640
You need to recover.

217
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:57,360
Then we'll find a way to escape.

218
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:13,560
You look much brighter and stronger, sir.

219
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,560
Keep fighting.

220
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:21,840
Sir.

221
00:18:22,920 --> 00:18:24,280
You can move.

222
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:29,320
It's not just my hand.
I can move my legs too.

223
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:34,040
You can talk too!
Hathaya, did you hear that?

224
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:36,120
He sure can move.

225
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:44,760
Wait. Don't tell me you all--

226
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:46,400
Yes, Daddy.

227
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:48,920
Great-Grandpa has been able to talk

228
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:51,320
and move for a while now.

229
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:53,840
But Aunt Hathaya

230
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:55,960
told us to keep it a secret.

231
00:18:58,200 --> 00:19:00,480
I've been dying

232
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:02,200
to tell you.

233
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:05,200
But Miss Hathaya strictly forbade it.

234
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:07,040
I don't understand.

235
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:10,760
-Why hide it from me?
-I wanted Grandpa

236
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:13,040
to get stronger first.

237
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:15,360
I wanted you to see him healthy

238
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:16,960
and get all excited like this.

239
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:19,800
And I was right.

240
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:22,320
You can't hide it at all.

241
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:25,000
You really wanted to see it?

242
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:29,480
Looks like I'm the third wheel now.

243
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:33,120
Grandpa.

244
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:36,520
Ramil has everything ready.

245
00:19:36,600 --> 00:19:38,920
You need to keep up with
your physical therapy.

246
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,360
Then you can attend the opening
of the development.

247
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:47,120
I'll be there.

248
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:58,200
You can stay home
and take care of Mr. Pichai.

249
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:59,800
I can handle things here.

250
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:02,240
Aunt Chamoi and Aunt Ann are helping.

251
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:04,320
Papang is there too.
So I feel even better.

252
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:06,360
And I need to sort out the accounts again.

253
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:07,600
That's good.

254
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:09,680
You're the only one he really trusts.

255
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:11,440
Once I finish,

256
00:20:11,520 --> 00:20:13,400
I'll help clean your office too.

257
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:14,680
It's probably a mess.

258
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:17,240
No, that's okay.

259
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:20,040
I already cleaned it.

260
00:20:22,440 --> 00:20:24,080
You don't have to be polite.

261
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:25,720
I'm not.

262
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:28,120
I mean Max and I

263
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:31,200
cleaned it already. Seriously. Spotless.

264
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:36,840
Men can't be trusted with cleaning.

265
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:40,080
You're never as thorough as women.

266
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:44,560
It really is clean.

267
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:47,400
I even brought in extra people to help.

268
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,000
Anyway…

269
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:51,080
I should go.

270
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:08,360
What are you hiding in there, Ramil?

271
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:10,040
HOME FOR SALE

272
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:11,400
Everyone.

273
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:13,720
Mr. Pichai is getting much stronger.

274
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:15,920
He's going to come
open the development himself.

275
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,000
So let's pick up the pace. Okay?

276
00:21:20,120 --> 00:21:22,400
Boss, Miss Hathaya went to your office.

277
00:21:24,760 --> 00:21:25,720
The secret's out.

278
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:30,720
Mom.

279
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:36,440
-Hathaya.
-What are you doing here?

280
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:38,800
I'm sorry, sweetheart.

281
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:42,200
Mom, wait.

282
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:43,320
I'm not a good person.

283
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:45,160
I don't want to cause you trouble anymore.

284
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:48,200
And you don't want to see me. I should go.

285
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:50,760
No. Explain this to me right now.

286
00:21:50,840 --> 00:21:52,840
What happened? Why are you here?

287
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:54,760
Aunt Hathai has been with us.

288
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:57,280
No point hiding it now.

289
00:21:58,240 --> 00:21:59,200
Ramil.

290
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:01,800
You gave my mom a job here?

291
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:03,640
After what happened that day,

292
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:07,400
I believed your mother had been framed.

293
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:12,920
So I found her a place to stay.

294
00:22:13,680 --> 00:22:15,920
She asked if she
could help clean the office

295
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:17,480
and the houses we're preparing.

296
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:20,400
After you went home,

297
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:23,760
she went to clean your office.

298
00:22:28,960 --> 00:22:30,600
I'm proud of you, sweetheart.

299
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:34,080
She has helped me

300
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:36,040
and the workers a lot.

301
00:22:36,120 --> 00:22:37,800
So everyone knew

302
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:40,720
except me?

303
00:22:44,520 --> 00:22:46,240
Don't blame Ramil.

304
00:22:47,120 --> 00:22:48,640
I asked him not to tell you.

305
00:22:50,040 --> 00:22:52,120
I just wanted to help you somehow.

306
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:55,520
I wanted to do something that
might make you proud of me.

307
00:22:57,360 --> 00:23:00,440
But now you know everything.

308
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:05,880
I should leave.
I don't want to bother you anymore.

309
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:09,240
Mom. Mom.

310
00:23:11,280 --> 00:23:12,640
I know everything now.

311
00:23:14,080 --> 00:23:16,760
Aunt Liu and Pong set you up.

312
00:23:19,280 --> 00:23:22,280
I was still wrong.

313
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:25,600
I broke my promise.

314
00:23:26,840 --> 00:23:28,520
I couldn't control myself.

315
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:36,400
Mom.

316
00:23:37,720 --> 00:23:39,800
Can you give yourself another chance?

317
00:23:42,440 --> 00:23:44,600
You don't have to promise me anything.

318
00:23:46,280 --> 00:23:48,000
Just give yourself another chance.

319
00:23:49,680 --> 00:23:51,480
And give me one too.

320
00:23:54,680 --> 00:23:57,440
I know you want to be a good mother to me.

321
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:03,040
I'm still your mother, right?

322
00:24:04,760 --> 00:24:06,520
I only have one mother.

323
00:24:07,920 --> 00:24:09,320
And her name is Hathai.

324
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:23,280
Hathaya… My girl.

325
00:24:48,560 --> 00:24:49,720
Grandpa.

326
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:51,840
I want to ask your permission

327
00:24:52,400 --> 00:24:54,720
for Mom to come live here with me.

328
00:24:56,080 --> 00:24:59,720
I know the truth now.

329
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:01,920
Mom was framed.

330
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:04,680
Aunt Liu and Chayanee were behind it.

331
00:25:05,840 --> 00:25:07,720
Please forgive her, Grandpa.

332
00:25:09,360 --> 00:25:10,280
What?

333
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:14,280
Did you lose your voice?
Why must your daughter speak for you?

334
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:26,120
Father, please give me one more chance.

335
00:25:27,640 --> 00:25:30,160
I want to come back and take care of you

336
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:32,120
and everyone here.

337
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:35,880
And I want to be with my daughter.

338
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:37,840
How do I know

339
00:25:38,360 --> 00:25:40,520
you won't cause trouble again?

340
00:25:46,400 --> 00:25:48,960
You once called me a parasite.

341
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:54,480
And you were right.

342
00:25:56,440 --> 00:25:58,040
I lived off other people.

343
00:25:58,880 --> 00:26:00,800
The moment someone
stopped being useful to me,

344
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:03,440
I abandoned them

345
00:26:03,520 --> 00:26:05,440
and found someone else.

346
00:26:08,920 --> 00:26:11,320
I never did anything for myself.

347
00:26:18,120 --> 00:26:21,320
When my own daughter

348
00:26:22,320 --> 00:26:24,160
threw me out,

349
00:26:26,240 --> 00:26:28,160
I finally had to think about everything.

350
00:26:28,760 --> 00:26:30,360
And I realized

351
00:26:31,040 --> 00:26:33,640
my life had no value at all.

352
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:38,400
I want another chance
to make things right.

353
00:26:42,200 --> 00:26:44,200
I want to start over.

354
00:26:45,840 --> 00:26:47,720
I want to take care of you.

355
00:26:48,400 --> 00:26:51,800
Take care of everyone here.
And take care of my daughter.

356
00:26:53,080 --> 00:26:54,720
Please give me one more chance.

357
00:27:05,120 --> 00:27:07,280
I don't think I can give you
what you're asking for.

358
00:27:16,680 --> 00:27:18,960
I don't have any authority anymore.

359
00:27:22,520 --> 00:27:24,800
I already made a new will.

360
00:27:29,960 --> 00:27:32,880
I left everything I own…

361
00:27:35,080 --> 00:27:36,640
including this house…

362
00:27:39,440 --> 00:27:40,840
to Hathaya.

363
00:27:49,040 --> 00:27:50,560
So if you want to live here,

364
00:27:52,120 --> 00:27:53,880
you'll have to ask the owner of the house.

365
00:27:58,360 --> 00:27:59,960
Grandpa.

366
00:28:05,440 --> 00:28:07,760
Thank you so much.

367
00:28:14,160 --> 00:28:15,760
Mom, come live with me.

368
00:28:37,840 --> 00:28:39,840
Sorry, the number
that you've dialed cannot--

369
00:28:40,720 --> 00:28:42,000
Ramil.

370
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:44,520
Have you been able to reach Raiwin?

371
00:28:45,120 --> 00:28:45,960
No.

372
00:28:46,680 --> 00:28:48,320
I'm not even sure he still

373
00:28:48,400 --> 00:28:49,520
uses the same number.

374
00:28:50,440 --> 00:28:51,440
What are you thinking?

375
00:28:52,720 --> 00:28:53,760
I…

376
00:28:54,920 --> 00:28:57,800
want you to ask him to turn himself in.

377
00:28:58,560 --> 00:29:00,720
The day I saw

378
00:29:00,800 --> 00:29:02,760
Raiwin about to kill Nuchwara…

379
00:29:03,360 --> 00:29:04,840
when Papang stopped him,

380
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:07,200
I saw the look in Raiwin's eyes.

381
00:29:08,800 --> 00:29:11,960
I could tell he cares
about how Papang feels.

382
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:17,240
Even if Raiwin won't openly
accept Papang as his son,

383
00:29:18,280 --> 00:29:20,240
if he spends time with him,

384
00:29:22,160 --> 00:29:24,440
I believe there's still
a father's heart inside him.

385
00:29:26,080 --> 00:29:28,800
Saksit raised Raiwin

386
00:29:30,160 --> 00:29:31,720
through aggression.

387
00:29:33,200 --> 00:29:34,920
Raiwin wants a family.

388
00:29:35,840 --> 00:29:37,640
And he wants to raise his son to be good.

389
00:29:39,880 --> 00:29:40,880
You may be right.

390
00:29:41,920 --> 00:29:44,080
Raiwin isn't naturally aggressive.

391
00:29:44,680 --> 00:29:45,920
His father pressured him.

392
00:29:47,360 --> 00:29:48,760
But how can you be sure

393
00:29:49,760 --> 00:29:51,120
Raiwin loves Papang?

394
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:53,960
If he didn't love Papang,

395
00:29:54,040 --> 00:29:56,280
he would have killed Nuchwara.

396
00:30:01,560 --> 00:30:03,280
Papang may love me as his father,

397
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:06,280
but I still want him

398
00:30:07,080 --> 00:30:08,760
to be with his biological father.

399
00:30:09,640 --> 00:30:11,600
I understand what Papang feels.

400
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:15,280
I was separated from my father too.

401
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:21,000
I'll send Raiwin a message.
Maybe he'll answer.

402
00:30:21,720 --> 00:30:22,560
Yes.

403
00:30:28,120 --> 00:30:31,040
Raiwin, I want to help you.

404
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:34,440
No one can help me.

405
00:30:35,840 --> 00:30:39,440
I'll help you with your case and
try to reduce the sentence.

406
00:30:48,480 --> 00:30:51,280
If you keep running, you'll be
running for the rest of your life.

407
00:30:52,040 --> 00:30:53,680
How do you even know you'll get away?

408
00:30:58,680 --> 00:31:01,480
Your son is waiting for you.

409
00:31:13,800 --> 00:31:15,360
RAIWIN

410
00:31:17,960 --> 00:31:19,160
Raiwin's calling.

411
00:31:21,040 --> 00:31:21,880
Hello.

412
00:31:23,160 --> 00:31:25,920
Raiwin. You need to meet me.

413
00:31:27,040 --> 00:31:28,560
I'll take you to turn yourself in.

414
00:31:29,560 --> 00:31:30,760
Bring your father too.

415
00:31:35,440 --> 00:31:36,440
Where were you?

416
00:31:38,440 --> 00:31:39,480
The bathroom.

417
00:31:40,080 --> 00:31:42,720
Who were you talking to
on the phone in the bathroom?

418
00:31:42,800 --> 00:31:45,280
I called Chayanee.

419
00:31:45,360 --> 00:31:47,720
I told her to find money for us

420
00:31:47,800 --> 00:31:49,160
so we can all escape together.

421
00:31:49,240 --> 00:31:51,840
You're planning to run away with them?

422
00:31:52,440 --> 00:31:53,560
No, Dad.

423
00:31:53,640 --> 00:31:56,120
I'm just tricking Chayanee
into bringing us the money.

424
00:31:56,640 --> 00:31:58,120
Then you and I will escape.

425
00:32:03,040 --> 00:32:05,720
That's more like it.

426
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:08,440
Now you're acting like my son.

427
00:32:09,440 --> 00:32:13,000
Tell them to bring the money
as soon as possible.

428
00:32:13,080 --> 00:32:14,680
I'm sick of this place.

429
00:32:23,680 --> 00:32:24,720
Ramil.

430
00:32:27,360 --> 00:32:29,520
Are you sure Raiwin will actually show up?

431
00:32:29,600 --> 00:32:32,560
I believe he really wants
to turn himself in.

432
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:34,680
Or he wouldn't have called.

433
00:32:35,200 --> 00:32:37,800
But he asked me

434
00:32:37,880 --> 00:32:39,200
not to tell the police yet.

435
00:32:39,800 --> 00:32:41,840
He wants me to take him
to see Papang first

436
00:32:42,440 --> 00:32:43,720
and apologize to Nuchwara.

437
00:32:44,600 --> 00:32:45,720
Then he'll turn himself in.

438
00:32:47,600 --> 00:32:50,360
-I'm coming with you.
-No. It's dangerous.

439
00:32:50,440 --> 00:32:51,720
I'm worried about you.

440
00:32:52,400 --> 00:32:54,440
And maybe I can help somehow.

441
00:32:54,960 --> 00:32:57,360
Two people are better than one.

442
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:06,040
Dad.

443
00:33:06,120 --> 00:33:07,720
It's almost time. We should go.

444
00:33:07,800 --> 00:33:11,040
Wait. Hold on.

445
00:33:11,880 --> 00:33:14,920
You said Chayanee and her mom

446
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:16,640
ran from police over Pichai.

447
00:33:18,520 --> 00:33:21,040
Where are they supposed
to get money for us?

448
00:33:21,560 --> 00:33:23,800
Think.

449
00:33:23,880 --> 00:33:27,320
Chayanee said she still
has some savings left.

450
00:33:27,840 --> 00:33:30,280
Good. Then pack up.

451
00:33:30,360 --> 00:33:31,320
Let's go.

452
00:33:31,840 --> 00:33:33,160
I'm sick of this place.

453
00:33:33,240 --> 00:33:34,800
Come on. Pack everything.

454
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:39,160
Who are you calling?

455
00:33:39,240 --> 00:33:40,720
Raiwin.

456
00:33:41,240 --> 00:33:42,800
Why?

457
00:33:42,880 --> 00:33:44,680
We don't have any money left to give him.

458
00:33:44,760 --> 00:33:46,920
I'll lie and tell him I do.

459
00:33:47,520 --> 00:33:49,200
Then I'll make him help us escape.

460
00:33:49,280 --> 00:33:51,360
And if they realize you're lying,

461
00:33:51,440 --> 00:33:53,240
they'll kill us.

462
00:33:53,840 --> 00:33:55,320
I'm not afraid of them.

463
00:33:56,280 --> 00:33:57,920
If they try to hurt me,

464
00:33:59,400 --> 00:34:00,880
we can fight to the death.

465
00:34:02,600 --> 00:34:04,240
I have nothing left to lose.

466
00:34:14,159 --> 00:34:15,800
Raiwin, your phone.

467
00:34:17,400 --> 00:34:18,400
Raiwin.

468
00:34:21,080 --> 00:34:22,239
Your phone is ringing.

469
00:34:24,520 --> 00:34:25,760
Who is it?

470
00:34:27,239 --> 00:34:28,480
A scammer.

471
00:34:28,560 --> 00:34:30,880
Oh?

472
00:34:30,960 --> 00:34:33,560
Those people are terrible.
They only fool idiots.

473
00:34:33,639 --> 00:34:35,800
Good thing someone like me isn't stupid.

474
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:40,760
CHAYANEE

475
00:34:41,360 --> 00:34:44,600
-Who is it now?
-Same people. Scammer.

476
00:34:44,679 --> 00:34:47,679
Block them next time. Understand?

477
00:34:48,800 --> 00:34:51,239
-It's time, Dad. Let's go.
-Fine.

478
00:34:56,880 --> 00:34:59,160
Raiwin isn't answering.
I can't reach him at all.

479
00:34:59,760 --> 00:35:01,240
He probably turned off his phone.

480
00:35:01,840 --> 00:35:03,640
Don't depend on those people anymore.

481
00:35:04,240 --> 00:35:06,360
Then what am I supposed to do?

482
00:35:06,440 --> 00:35:08,560
Go back and ask Grandpa for help.

483
00:35:08,640 --> 00:35:09,800
Or…

484
00:35:09,880 --> 00:35:12,120
ask Hathaya.

485
00:35:12,200 --> 00:35:13,560
That woman is soft-hearted.

486
00:35:14,160 --> 00:35:15,600
Grandpa adores her.

487
00:35:15,680 --> 00:35:17,400
Whatever she asks for,

488
00:35:17,480 --> 00:35:18,520
he gives her.

489
00:35:18,600 --> 00:35:20,840
Stop saying her name.

490
00:35:20,920 --> 00:35:22,000
I hate her.

491
00:35:22,600 --> 00:35:24,320
Then what are you going to do?

492
00:35:33,600 --> 00:35:36,320
Where are Chayanee and her mother?

493
00:35:37,280 --> 00:35:38,960
We're meeting them inside, Dad.

494
00:35:40,760 --> 00:35:43,000
Fine. Then go get the money.

495
00:35:43,080 --> 00:35:44,240
I'll wait in the car.

496
00:35:45,320 --> 00:35:46,760
Dad, come inside with me.

497
00:35:47,920 --> 00:35:50,360
Why do I have to go in

498
00:35:50,440 --> 00:35:51,760
just to collect money?

499
00:35:51,840 --> 00:35:53,160
You can bring it out here.

500
00:35:54,680 --> 00:35:58,000
They know you have
the connections to help us escape.

501
00:35:58,760 --> 00:36:02,640
They want to hear it directly from you.
If you go in and reassure Chayanee,

502
00:36:02,720 --> 00:36:04,480
she'll hand over the money.

503
00:36:05,080 --> 00:36:06,000
I'm not going.

504
00:36:06,520 --> 00:36:09,880
Tell them if they don't trust me,

505
00:36:10,640 --> 00:36:13,400
-then they don't need my help.
-Dad, please come inside.

506
00:36:13,480 --> 00:36:15,400
You go get the money.

507
00:36:15,480 --> 00:36:18,120
Hurry up. Before the police
come and arrest us.

508
00:36:18,200 --> 00:36:20,520
Go.

509
00:36:29,200 --> 00:36:31,640
Who are you calling now?

510
00:36:32,360 --> 00:36:34,160
Raiwin won't answer me.

511
00:36:34,240 --> 00:36:36,000
So I'll call his father.

512
00:36:36,600 --> 00:36:38,440
I'll trick him into helping us escape.

513
00:36:41,120 --> 00:36:42,880
Chayanee, why are you calling me?

514
00:36:43,560 --> 00:36:45,200
Your son won't answer me.

515
00:36:45,280 --> 00:36:46,920
So I had to call you.

516
00:36:47,600 --> 00:36:48,720
Wait.

517
00:36:49,920 --> 00:36:52,680
Raiwin arranged to meet you for the money.

518
00:36:52,760 --> 00:36:54,880
He just went inside to see you.

519
00:36:54,960 --> 00:36:57,120
How could Raiwin be coming to see me?

520
00:36:57,200 --> 00:36:59,840
He won't answer my calls.
He even blocked my number.

521
00:37:00,440 --> 00:37:01,440
Then who is he meeting?

522
00:37:02,640 --> 00:37:04,160
I called because I want you

523
00:37:04,240 --> 00:37:05,640
to come get the money

524
00:37:05,720 --> 00:37:07,640
and help Mom and me escape.

525
00:37:09,960 --> 00:37:11,280
I'll call you back.

526
00:37:11,360 --> 00:37:14,520
Where are you? Hello?

527
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:17,440
What did they say?

528
00:37:18,040 --> 00:37:19,520
Raiwin claimed he arranged to meet me.

529
00:37:20,440 --> 00:37:22,240
But I have no idea
who he's actually meeting.

530
00:37:36,640 --> 00:37:39,080
I'm going to meet Raiwin. Wait here.

531
00:37:40,120 --> 00:37:42,760
Be careful. I'm worried about you.

532
00:37:42,840 --> 00:37:44,600
I'll take good care of myself.

533
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:49,120
And I'll come back smiling for you. Okay?

534
00:37:51,960 --> 00:37:52,800
Wait here.

535
00:38:01,360 --> 00:38:02,360
Where's your father?

536
00:38:03,160 --> 00:38:04,240
He won't come inside.

537
00:38:05,680 --> 00:38:07,800
Do you think he knows
you're turning yourself in?

538
00:38:08,400 --> 00:38:09,480
I don't think so.

539
00:38:11,120 --> 00:38:14,000
What do we do, Ramil?
How do we get him to turn himself in too?

540
00:38:14,760 --> 00:38:15,920
If he won't come to us,

541
00:38:16,760 --> 00:38:17,720
we go to him.

542
00:38:18,600 --> 00:38:20,520
We have to persuade him to do so.

543
00:38:22,160 --> 00:38:23,560
He won't surrender.

544
00:38:24,440 --> 00:38:25,760
He refuses to die in prison.

545
00:38:26,720 --> 00:38:27,920
We still have to try.

546
00:38:29,040 --> 00:38:30,000
I'll come with you.

547
00:38:32,600 --> 00:38:33,600
Let's go.

548
00:38:46,440 --> 00:38:47,520
Dad's gone.

549
00:38:48,560 --> 00:38:49,600
Do you think he ran?

550
00:38:57,000 --> 00:38:58,000
Ramil, watch out!

551
00:38:59,240 --> 00:39:00,760
Dad!

552
00:39:00,840 --> 00:39:03,240
Don't move.

553
00:39:03,320 --> 00:39:06,480
All of you ruined my life.
You're all going to die.

554
00:39:06,560 --> 00:39:08,280
You ruined your own life.

555
00:39:09,080 --> 00:39:12,120
No one forced you to do evil.
No one forced you to steal.

556
00:39:12,880 --> 00:39:15,320
You messed up.
Now you have to face the consequences.

557
00:39:15,400 --> 00:39:16,240
No.

558
00:39:17,040 --> 00:39:18,800
Ramil, don't lecture me.

559
00:39:22,880 --> 00:39:23,720
Dad.

560
00:39:25,520 --> 00:39:26,960
Enough.

561
00:39:27,560 --> 00:39:29,320
Raiwin, you too.

562
00:39:29,920 --> 00:39:31,960
You said you were going to help me.

563
00:39:32,560 --> 00:39:35,760
But you sided with them.

564
00:39:36,360 --> 00:39:37,720
You're saving yourself.

565
00:39:39,160 --> 00:39:40,320
No, Dad.

566
00:39:42,160 --> 00:39:43,840
I never planned to betray you.

567
00:39:46,440 --> 00:39:48,280
I'm trying to help you.

568
00:39:48,360 --> 00:39:50,320
Don't pretend this is about helping me.

569
00:39:50,880 --> 00:39:52,640
You're saving yourself.

570
00:39:54,600 --> 00:39:55,640
I've tried

571
00:39:57,520 --> 00:39:58,920
to help you with everything.

572
00:40:00,840 --> 00:40:01,880
All these years,

573
00:40:02,600 --> 00:40:05,640
whatever you ordered me to do, I did.

574
00:40:08,760 --> 00:40:11,840
You even forced me to kill Uncle Anon.

575
00:40:12,920 --> 00:40:14,000
Shut up.

576
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:18,960
Move.

577
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:21,200
Enough, Dad.

578
00:40:22,120 --> 00:40:24,800
I'm grown now. I have a son.

579
00:40:26,360 --> 00:40:28,440
Let me make my own decisions.

580
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:33,400
It's humiliating.
I became Subdistrict Chief,

581
00:40:34,400 --> 00:40:35,960
but I was still a parasite

582
00:40:36,920 --> 00:40:39,760
living off your influence
and obeying your every order.

583
00:40:41,720 --> 00:40:44,520
Even an ordinary villager

584
00:40:44,600 --> 00:40:47,800
has more dignity than I do.
More dignity than you.

585
00:40:47,880 --> 00:40:49,800
Stop talking. Shut up.

586
00:40:50,880 --> 00:40:52,000
Move.

587
00:40:54,600 --> 00:40:56,600
I'm going to kill
every one of these parasites.

588
00:40:58,440 --> 00:40:59,280
Move.

589
00:41:03,680 --> 00:41:05,200
Let me ask you one thing.

590
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:11,000
I'm Raiwin. Your son.

591
00:41:14,800 --> 00:41:16,400
Did you ever love me?

592
00:41:18,360 --> 00:41:21,840
You betrayed me.

593
00:41:22,600 --> 00:41:24,520
-Move.
-Well?

594
00:41:26,080 --> 00:41:28,680
I said move.

595
00:41:28,760 --> 00:41:31,480
And don't come any closer.

596
00:41:35,080 --> 00:41:38,160
I said move.
I'm going to kill all of them.

597
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:40,080
Did you ever love me?

598
00:41:41,360 --> 00:41:42,480
Ever?

599
00:41:42,560 --> 00:41:45,720
No. No.

600
00:41:45,800 --> 00:41:48,000
Don't come closer. Stay away from me.

601
00:41:49,160 --> 00:41:50,080
Move.

602
00:41:50,680 --> 00:41:51,760
Step closer and I'll shoot.

603
00:41:53,880 --> 00:41:55,400
Don't come closer. Don't.

604
00:41:56,040 --> 00:41:59,640
-I'm your son. Do you love me?
-No…

605
00:42:01,480 --> 00:42:03,400
Stay away from me. I said move.

606
00:42:04,400 --> 00:42:05,320
Enough, Dad.

607
00:42:05,400 --> 00:42:07,920
-Please. Did you ever love me?
-Stay back!

608
00:42:14,360 --> 00:42:15,200
-Enough, Dad.
-Stop.

609
00:42:28,800 --> 00:42:30,240
Give me the gun.

610
00:42:30,320 --> 00:42:31,800
Stop.

611
00:42:31,880 --> 00:42:34,040
Let go. I said give me the gun.

612
00:42:34,120 --> 00:42:35,400
Give it to me.

613
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:42,200
Dad, enough.

614
00:42:42,800 --> 00:42:45,280
Please, Dad.

615
00:42:57,800 --> 00:42:58,960
Hey.

616
00:42:59,520 --> 00:43:00,520
Raiwin, how bad is it?

617
00:43:01,720 --> 00:43:02,800
Ramil.

618
00:43:02,880 --> 00:43:04,880
We need to get him to the hospital.

619
00:43:05,480 --> 00:43:06,680
Come on.

620
00:43:06,760 --> 00:43:09,040
-Can you stand?
-Easy.

621
00:43:28,720 --> 00:43:30,000
I don't even know

622
00:43:31,200 --> 00:43:32,640
whether surviving

623
00:43:33,960 --> 00:43:36,040
was good luck or bad luck.

624
00:43:39,280 --> 00:43:41,480
It hurts knowing…

625
00:43:42,760 --> 00:43:44,360
Dad never loved me.

626
00:43:46,280 --> 00:43:49,520
He was willing to kill his own son.

627
00:43:51,680 --> 00:43:52,640
Come on.

628
00:43:54,320 --> 00:43:55,480
Don't dwell on it.

629
00:43:56,040 --> 00:43:58,720
You'll only hurt yourself more.

630
00:44:01,040 --> 00:44:03,640
I'm sorry this happened to you.

631
00:44:05,480 --> 00:44:08,480
None of us chooses to be
born into situations like this.

632
00:44:09,560 --> 00:44:12,840
You, Ramil,

633
00:44:14,560 --> 00:44:15,680
or me…

634
00:44:18,240 --> 00:44:20,160
all of us have had terrible things

635
00:44:20,240 --> 00:44:22,320
happen in our families.

636
00:44:23,440 --> 00:44:25,760
No family is perfect.

637
00:44:27,040 --> 00:44:29,040
No parent is perfect.

638
00:44:30,600 --> 00:44:32,040
And we are

639
00:44:32,720 --> 00:44:34,520
not perfect either.

640
00:44:37,360 --> 00:44:39,640
From a Buddhist perspective,

641
00:44:41,040 --> 00:44:43,200
everything happens according to karma.

642
00:44:43,960 --> 00:44:46,720
We're in each other's lives
because of karma.

643
00:44:47,600 --> 00:44:48,960
But what matters is that

644
00:44:49,480 --> 00:44:52,000
we don't tie our entire lives
to someone else,

645
00:44:53,600 --> 00:44:55,200
not even the people who gave us life.

646
00:44:57,160 --> 00:44:59,080
Good or bad, we choose who we are.

647
00:45:00,680 --> 00:45:02,520
I think you're fortunate.

648
00:45:04,360 --> 00:45:05,920
You're still alive.

649
00:45:07,560 --> 00:45:09,000
You can still set things right

650
00:45:10,240 --> 00:45:11,760
and be with the people you love.

651
00:45:17,280 --> 00:45:18,320
I know

652
00:45:20,280 --> 00:45:21,560
you care about Papang.

653
00:45:23,400 --> 00:45:25,000
And Papang is probably

654
00:45:26,440 --> 00:45:27,640
waiting for you to hold him.

655
00:45:30,120 --> 00:45:31,800
Hathaya is right.

656
00:45:33,760 --> 00:45:35,280
I have a good younger brother.

657
00:45:40,080 --> 00:45:43,240
You've always helped me and forgiven me.

658
00:45:45,800 --> 00:45:47,400
I'm sorry, Ramil.

659
00:45:48,840 --> 00:45:50,840
I tried to hurt you in so many ways.

660
00:45:51,520 --> 00:45:53,880
I'm glad

661
00:45:55,840 --> 00:45:57,440
I finally have my big brother back.

662
00:46:09,280 --> 00:46:12,480
I think you can still be
a good father to Papang.

663
00:46:13,600 --> 00:46:15,560
I'm too ashamed to face him.

664
00:46:18,800 --> 00:46:20,400
I'm a terrible father.

665
00:46:24,040 --> 00:46:27,360
I almost killed his mother.

666
00:46:31,240 --> 00:46:33,680
I'll explain things to Papang.

667
00:46:35,880 --> 00:46:38,320
I believe he can forgive you.

668
00:46:42,360 --> 00:46:44,560
Great-Grandpa, walk toward me.

669
00:46:47,400 --> 00:46:49,440
One more step.

670
00:46:50,840 --> 00:46:52,400
Alright.

671
00:46:52,480 --> 00:46:54,640
Great-Grandpa, you're the literal GOAT!

672
00:46:56,240 --> 00:46:58,800
What did you say? A goat?

673
00:46:59,560 --> 00:47:01,760
It means you're the greatest of all time!

674
00:47:04,880 --> 00:47:08,560
My Papang is the GOAT too.

675
00:47:08,640 --> 00:47:10,840
And the cutest too.

676
00:47:24,200 --> 00:47:25,200
Alright.

677
00:47:25,800 --> 00:47:27,040
Okay.

678
00:47:27,880 --> 00:47:29,040
-Let's go back.
-Yes.

679
00:47:29,120 --> 00:47:30,120
Go, Mom.

680
00:47:42,360 --> 00:47:43,280
Papang.

681
00:47:45,480 --> 00:47:47,360
Daddy Raiwin isn't feeling well.

682
00:47:48,920 --> 00:47:51,000
Will you come visit him with us?

683
00:47:51,720 --> 00:47:53,960
But I'm scared.

684
00:47:57,480 --> 00:47:59,040
Are you very scared?

685
00:47:59,640 --> 00:48:02,560
Very, very scared.

686
00:48:03,160 --> 00:48:06,040
Scared to the moon and back?

687
00:48:06,640 --> 00:48:09,320
The most scared ever.

688
00:48:09,920 --> 00:48:11,640
I'll tell you a secret.

689
00:48:11,720 --> 00:48:14,080
That day, a giant monster

690
00:48:14,160 --> 00:48:16,200
got inside Daddy Raiwin.

691
00:48:16,280 --> 00:48:19,040
That's why Daddy Raiwin
turned into a scary giant.

692
00:48:19,560 --> 00:48:22,760
But now he has defeated that giant.

693
00:48:23,600 --> 00:48:24,520
That's right.

694
00:48:24,600 --> 00:48:27,080
Daddy Raiwin is himself again now.

695
00:48:27,680 --> 00:48:29,920
And he's hurt pretty badly.

696
00:48:30,520 --> 00:48:32,640
He needs special medicine to get better.

697
00:48:33,240 --> 00:48:36,480
Then you and Aunt Hathaya
should buy some medicine

698
00:48:36,560 --> 00:48:40,000
and take it to Daddy Raiwin.

699
00:48:40,640 --> 00:48:41,840
The problem is

700
00:48:41,920 --> 00:48:44,920
you can't buy this medicine
anywhere in the world.

701
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:46,280
Because it's magic medicine.

702
00:48:46,880 --> 00:48:48,520
But do you know where it is?

703
00:48:50,280 --> 00:48:51,440
Right here.

704
00:48:53,200 --> 00:48:55,440
If you want Daddy Raiwin to get better,

705
00:48:55,520 --> 00:48:57,560
all you have to do is put

706
00:48:57,640 --> 00:48:58,920
your chest against his.

707
00:48:59,000 --> 00:49:00,880
Then he'll start getting better.

708
00:49:03,160 --> 00:49:06,400
Please. Come help us heal your dad.

709
00:49:08,040 --> 00:49:09,040
Please?

710
00:49:09,840 --> 00:49:12,080
I'll take the magic medicine

711
00:49:12,160 --> 00:49:13,920
to help Daddy Raiwin.

712
00:49:14,520 --> 00:49:16,840
That's my boy. You're amazing.

713
00:49:17,520 --> 00:49:18,480
So brave.

714
00:49:33,520 --> 00:49:34,960
I never meant to hurt you.

715
00:49:35,040 --> 00:49:37,040
You were pointing a gun at me.

716
00:49:37,120 --> 00:49:39,640
A father willing to kill his own son?

717
00:49:39,720 --> 00:49:42,640
And what if it were me?
What would you do then?

718
00:49:42,720 --> 00:49:44,640
Just don't betray me, Mom.

719
00:49:45,400 --> 00:49:47,400
‎NEXT EPISODE

720
00:51:47,240 --> 00:51:49,240
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
